{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Your name is Jacob.</b> I now fulfill this name for you — that you alone shall endure, in the wake and aftermath of the destruction of all the other nations, as it says: כִּי אֶעֱשֶׂה כָלָה בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם וְאוֹתְךָ לֹא אֶעֱשֶׂה כָלָה (Jeremiah 46:28)." "<b>Your name shall no longer be called Jacob.</b> And when the import of the name Jacob is fulfilled — that you alone remain at the end, as it says: הֶן עָם לְבָדָד יִשְׁכֹּן (Numbers 23:9) — then the name Jacob will have no further significance." "<b>But Israel shall be your name.</b> That you shall rule over all who survive of the nations, as it says: וְקַרְקַר כָּל בְּנֵי שֵׁת (Numbers 24:17)." "<b>And He called his name Israel.</b> He blessed him that some measure of the import of the name Israel begin from now — that he may prevail against those who rise up against him even in a land not his own, as the Sages said (Sanhedrin 76a): כָּל מָקוֹם שֶׁהָלְכוּ נַעֲשׂוּ שָׂרִים לַאֲדוֹנֵיהֶם."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:24.687062153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}